	<special_qualities>
		<!-- Visible All "Special Ability" Ability Objects -->
		<special_quality>
			<name>Dragon Age Category - Great Wyrm</name>
			<description></description>
			<type>SPECIALQUALITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect>NAME: Dragon Age Category - Great Wyrm</aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - </source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Bite</name>
			<description>This is a primary attack that deals the indicated damage plus 1-1/2 times the dragon&#39;s Strength bonus (even though it has more than one attack). A dragon&#39;s bite attack has reach as if the creature were one size category larger (+10 feet for Colossal dragons).</description>
			<type>RACEABILITY.SPECIALQUALITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - </source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Blindsense (Ex)</name>
			<description>Range 60 ft.; Other creatures have blindsense, a lesser ability that lets the creature notice things it cannot see, but without the precision of blindsight. The creature with blindsense usually does not need to make Spot or Listen checks to notice and locate creatures within range of its blindsense ability, provided that it has line of effect to that creature. Any opponent the creature cannot see has total concealment (50% miss chance) against the creature with blindsense, and the blindsensing creature still has the normal miss chance when attacking foes that have concealment. Visibility still affects the movement of a creature with blindsense. A creature with blindsense is still denied its Dexterity bonus to Armor Class against attacks from creatures it cannot see.</description>
			<type>SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY.VISION</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect>Vision: Blindsense 60 ft.</aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - </source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Breath Weapon (Su)</name>
			<description>Using a breath weapon is a standard action. A dragon can use its breath weapon once every 1d4 rounds, even if it possesses more than one breath weapon. A breath weapon always starts at an intersection adjacent to the dragon and extends in a direction of the dragon&#39;s choice. Breath weapons come in two shapes, lines and cones, whose areas vary with the dragon&#39;s size. If a breath weapon deals damage, those caught in the area can attempt Reflex saves to take half damage. The save DC against a breath weapon is 10 + 1/2 dragon&#39;s HD + dragon&#39;s Con modifier. Saves against various breath weapons use the same DC; the type of saving throw is noted in the variety descriptions. A dragon can use its breath weapon when it is grappling or being grappled.</description>
			<type>RACEABILITY.SPECIALQUALITY.SUPERNATURAL</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - </source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Change Shape (Su)</name>
			<description>A very young or older gold dragon can assume any animal or humanoid form three times per day as if using polymorph.</description>
			<type>SPECIALQUALITY.SUPERNATURAL</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Bestiary, p.108</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Claw</name>
			<description>These primary attacks deal the indicated damage plus the dragon&#39;s Strength bonus.</description>
			<type>RACEABILITY.SPECIALQUALITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - </source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Damage Reduction</name>
			<description>Dragons gain damage reduction as they age, as indicated on each dragon&#39;s specific entry. Their natural weapons are treated as magic weapons for the purpose of overcoming damage reduction.</description>
			<type>RACEABILITY.SPECIALQUALITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - </source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Darkvision (Ex)</name>
			<description>Range 120 ft.; Darkvision is the extraordinary ability to see with no light source at all, out to a range specified for the creature. Darkvision is black and white only (colors cannot be discerned). It does not allow characters to see anything that they could not see otherwise-invisible objects are still invisible, and illusions are still visible as what they seem to be. Likewise, darkvision subjects a creature to gaze attacks normally. The presence of light does not spoil darkvision.</description>
			<type>SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY.VISION</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect>Vision: Darkvision 120 ft.</aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - </source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Detect Gems (Sp)</name>
			<description>A young or older gold dragon can detect gems three times per day. This functions as locate object, but can only be used to locate gemstones.</description>
			<type>SPECIALQUALITY.SPELLLIKE.SENSE</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Bestiary, p.108</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Divine Aid (Sp)</name>
			<description>Once a week, a great wyrm gold dragon can call upon celestial powers for aid. This functions as a miracle.</description>
			<type>SPECIALQUALITY.SPELLLIKE</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Bestiary, p.108</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Dragon Senses (Ex)</name>
			<description>Dragons have darkvision 120 ft. and blindsense 60 ft. They see four times as well as a human in dim light and twice as well in normal light.</description>
			<type>RACEABILITY.SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - </source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Dragon Senses (Ex)</name>
			<description>Dragons have darkvision 120 ft. and blindsense 60 ft. They see four times as well as a human in dim light and twice as well in normal light.</description>
			<type>SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - </source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Fast Flight (Ex)</name>
			<description>A young or older gold dragon is treated as one size category larger when determining his fly speed.</description>
			<type>SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY.MODIFYMOVEMENT</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Bestiary, p.108</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Fire Aura (Su)</name>
			<description>An old or older gold dragon is surrounded by an aura of fire. All creatures within 10 feet of the dragon take 2d6 points of fire damage at the beginning of the dragon&#39;s turn. The dragon can activate or suppress this aura as a free action.</description>
			<type>SPECIALQUALITY.SUPERNATURAL.AURA</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect>Ability Benefit: (10 ft., 2d6 fire damage)</aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Bestiary, p.108</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Frightful Presence (Ex)</name>
			<description>A dragon&#39;s frightful presence has a range equal to 30 feet x the dragon&#39;s age category [360&#39;], but otherwise functions as detailed on page 300.</description>
			<type>RACEABILITY.SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - </source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Immunities (Ex)</name>
			<description>Every dragon is immune to sleep and paralysis. In addition, a dragon is immune to one or two additional forms of attack no matter what its age, as given in its description.</description>
			<type>RACEABILITY.SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - </source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Immunity to Fire (Ex)</name>
			<description>You never take fire damage.</description>
			<type>SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY.IMMUNITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect>Immunity: Fire</aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Bestiary, p.301</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Immunity to Magical Sleep (Ex)</name>
			<description>You are never subject to magic sleep effects.</description>
			<type>SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY.IMMUNITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect>Immunity: Magical Sleep</aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Bestiary, p.301</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Immunity to Paralysis (Ex)</name>
			<description>You can never be paralyzed.</description>
			<type>SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY.IMMUNITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect>Immunity: Paralysis</aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Bestiary, p.301</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Low-Light Vision (Ex)</name>
			<description>You can see x4 as far as humans in low illumination. Characters with low-light vision have eyes that are so sensitive to light that they can see twice as far as normal in dim light. Low-Light Vision is color vision. A spellcaster with low-light vision can read a scroll as long as even the tiniest candle flame is next to her as a source of light. Characters with low-light vision can see outdoors on a moonlit night as well as they can during the day.</description>
			<type>SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY.VISION</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect>Vision: Low-Light Vision</aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - </source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Luck (Sp)</name>
			<description>Once per day an adult or older gold dragon can touch a gem, usually one embedded in the dragon&#39;s hide, and enspell it to bring good luck. As long as the dragon carries the gem, it and every good creature within a given radius of it (120 ft.) receives a +1 luck bonus on all saving throws. If the dragon gives an enspelled gem to another creature, only that bearer gets the bonus. The effect lasts 1d3+12 hours. This ability is the equivalent of a 2nd-level spell.</description>
			<type>SPECIALQUALITY.SPELLLIKE.AURA</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Bestiary, p.108</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Spell-Like Abilities</name>
			<description>A dragon&#39;s caster level for its spelllike abilities is equal to its total Hit Dice.</description>
			<type>RACEABILITY.SPECIALQUALITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - </source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Spell Resistance (Ex)</name>
			<description>As dragons grow older, they become more resistant to spells and spell-like abilities, as indicated in the dragon descriptions. A dragon&#39;s SR is equal to 11 + its CR.</description>
			<type>RACEABILITY.SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - </source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Spells</name>
			<description>A dragon knows and casts arcane spells as a sorcerer of the level indicated in its specific description. Its caster level depends on its age, as shown for each type.</description>
			<type>RACEABILITY.SPECIALQUALITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - </source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Tail Slap</name>
			<description>The dragon can slap one foe each round with its tail. A tail slap is a secondary attack that deals the indicated damage plus 1-1/2 times the dragon&#39;s Strength bonus (this is an exception to the normal secondary attack rules).</description>
			<type>RACEABILITY.SPECIALQUALITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - </source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Vulnerability to Cold (Ex)</name>
			<description>You take half again as much (+50%) damage as normal from Cold, regardless of whether a saving throw is allowed, or if the save is a success or failure</description>
			<type>SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY.WEAKNESS.VULNERABILITYENERGY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Bestiary, p.305</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Wing</name>
			<description>The dragon can slam foes with its wings, even when flying. Wing attacks are secondary attacks that deal the indicated damage plus 1/2 the dragon&#39;s Strength bonus.</description>
			<type>RACEABILITY.SPECIALQUALITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - </source>
